# Playwright Conventions

## Auth

Stored session by default (`tests/auth.setup.ts` → `playwright/.auth/user.json`). UI login only when the test is the login page. API login (POST credentials, then inject the token) is for bulk setup, a one-off script, or a stale storageState.

```typescript
// Login-page test only
test.use({ storageState: { cookies: [], origins: [] } });
await new LoginPage(page).goto();
```

A feature spec does not call `/login` or write a password into source.

## Page Objects

One class per page or component in `pages/` (`LoginPage`, `ProgramsPage`, `NewProgramModal`). Locators are `readonly` in the constructor. Methods only go, click, fill, or submit. A page composes the components it contains. The spec states intent; every `expect` stays in `tests/`.

```typescript
const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
await programs.openNewProgramForm();
await expect(programs.newProgramNameField).toBeVisible();
```

## Locators

`getByRole`, then `getByLabel` or `getByPlaceholder`, then `getByText`, then `getByTestId` with a comment on why nothing higher worked. Narrow a multi-match with `.filter({ hasText })`.

```typescript
this.dialog = page.getByRole('dialog', { name: 'New Program' });
this.programNameField = this.dialog.getByLabel('Program Name');
this.createButton = this.dialog.getByRole('button', { name: 'Create' });
```

No CSS selectors, XPath, brittle copy, or `.first()` on several matches.

## Data and cleanup

Name each created row with `uniqueSuffix()` (`Date.now()` plus a counter from `tests/helpers/didaxis-programs.ts`). Import `test` from `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts` and call `trackProgram` with `data.id` from the real create response. The fixture deletes `DELETE /api/programs/<uuid>?purge=true` with `DIDAXIS_API_TOKEN`.

```typescript
import { expect, test } from '../fixtures/cleanup.fixture';
import { uniqueSuffix } from './helpers/didaxis-programs';

const programName = `Data Analytics 2026 ${uniqueSuffix()}`;
trackProgram(await programs.submitCreateProgram());
```

No manual `afterAll` cleanup, no hardcoded Bearer token, and no `trackProgram` on an id the test did not create.

## Waiting

Wait with a web-first assertion that retries: `expect(locator).toBeVisible()`, `.toBeEnabled()`, or `.toHaveText()`.

```typescript
await expect(programs.newProgramNameField).toBeVisible();
await expect(programs.newProgramCreateButton).toBeEnabled();
```

No `waitForTimeout`, and no one-shot `expect(await locator.isVisible()).toBe(true)`. A fixed sleep ends before the programs list refetches, and a boolean sampled once does not retry.

## Network mocking

Fulfill with `page.route` in the spec only the programs call that produces the UI state under test. Tag the test `{ tag: '@edge' }`. Assert copy already on the page object. Read the live page before writing the sentence. When the app renders nothing, assert `programs.heading` is visible and that no `pageerror` fired.

```typescript
test('empty list shows the empty state', { tag: '@edge' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/api/programs', async (route) => {
    const path = new URL(route.request().url()).pathname.replace(/\/$/, '');
    if (route.request().method() !== 'GET' || !path.endsWith('/programs')) {
      await route.continue();
      return;
    }
    await route.fulfill({
      status: 200,
      contentType: 'application/json',
      body: JSON.stringify({ data: [] }),
    });
  });
  const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
  await programs.goto();
  await expect(programs.emptyProgramsText).toBeVisible();
});
```

The same shape covers `503` on `PATCH /programs/<id>`, a `200` body that is not a program array, and `404` / `400` / `403` / `500` / `501` on save, plus `401` / `502` / `504` / `300` on list load.

Do not mock the endpoint the test claims to verify, fulfill `**/api/programs/**` for every method, `trackProgram` a mocked id, or assert a sentence the live page does not render (`Service Unavailable`).

## Accessibility

Scan in `tests/<feature>.a11y.spec.ts` through `expectNoAxeViolations` with tags `wcag2a` and `wcag2aa`. One `{ tag: '@a11y' }` per test. Run the keyboard path through the POM inside `runCiSoftA11y`. A real violation is an info report (rule id, impact, target, help URL) and must not fail CI.

```typescript
test('has no WCAG 2 A or AA violations', { tag: '@a11y' }, async ({ page }) => {
  const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
  await programs.goto();
  await expect(programs.heading).toBeVisible();
  await expectNoAxeViolations(page, { tags: ['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa'] });
});

test('Enter on New Program opens the dialog', { tag: '@a11y' }, async ({ page }) => {
  await runCiSoftA11y('programs-new-program-keyboard', async () => {
    const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
    await programs.goto();
    await expect(programs.newProgramButton).toBeFocused();
    await page.keyboard.press('Enter');
    await expect(programs.newProgramDialog).toBeVisible();
  });
});
```

No bare `expect(results.violations).toEqual([])` in the spec, no `.disableRules()`, and no `.include()` / `.exclude()` without a comment naming the noisy third-party widget.

## Anti-flake

Keep `fullyParallel: true`, `retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0` (never above 2), `trace: 'on-first-retry'`, `baseURL` from `DIDAXIS_URL`, `locale` `en-US`, and `timezoneId` `America/Toronto`. Serialize only the describe that shares one admin. Freeze a relative timestamp with `page.clock.install` before navigation. Page objects do not install the clock.

```typescript
test.describe('DS-1: Create new academic program', () => {
  test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial', timeout: 120_000 });

  test('creates a uniquely named program', async ({ programs, trackProgram }) => {
    const programName = `Data Analytics 2026 ${uniqueSuffix()}`;
    trackProgram(await programs.createProgram(programName, 'Full-stack web development program'));
    await expectProgramInList(programs, programName);
  });
});

test('row shows when the program was saved', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.clock.install({ time: new Date('2026-10-30T16:00:00') });
  const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
  await programs.goto();
  await expect(programs.programRow('Web Development')).toContainText('2 minutes ago');
});
```

Do not set `workers: 1`, `fullyParallel: false`, retries above 2, or another locale or timezone. Do not assert a relative label from `Date.now()` (`just now`, `2 minutes ago`, `today`).
